# Page 2 — The five proof-semantics classes

Each group is classified by inspecting the stored proof terms. Priority when several
apply: **deprecated > alias > rfl-variant > independent > unknown**.

| class | groups | meaning |
|---|---|---|
| alias | 1,671 | identical proof term — one is a copy/alias of another |
| independent | 1,266 | same statement, **distinct** proof trees |
| unknown | 353 | ≥1 member has no proof value (axiom/opaque/ctor/structural) |
| deprecated | 124 | ≥1 member carries `@[deprecated]` |
| rfl-variant | 22 | ≥1 proof is `rfl`/`trivial`, another is elaborated |

By syntax: **2,938** byte-identical statements,
**498** with a spelling delta, of which
**3** are pure hash collisions (see Page 9).

Pages 3–7 take each class in turn with 2–3 exemplars; Page 8 isolates the
non-autogenerated (user-written) duplicates; Page 9 dissects the hash collisions.
